---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base
  title="Property Management in Plano, Frisco, McKinney &amp; Allen | Ling Jordan"
  description="Residential and commercial property management across Collin County. Fifty doors under management, published fees, licensed oversight."
  path="/owners"
>
  <section class="wrap section narrow">
    <p class="eyebrow">Property management</p>
    <h1>Fifty doors, and a phone number that reaches a licensed agent.</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Most management companies route you to a portal ticket and a call center.
      When something goes wrong with your property, you talk to me.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="band">
    <div class="wrap section">
      <h2 style="margin-top:0">What it costs</h2>
      <p class="prose">
        Published, because most companies will not. If a competitor requires a
        form submission before telling you their management fee, that is worth
        noticing.
      </p>
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr><th scope="col">Service</th><th scope="col">Fee</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Monthly management</td><td>TODO-FEE% of collected rent</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Leasing fee (new tenant)</td><td>TODO-FEE</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Renewal fee</td><td>TODO-FEE</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Maintenance coordination</td><td>TODO-FEE</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Setup and onboarding</td><td>TODO-FEE</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Eviction coordination</td><td>TODO-FEE</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <p class="notice">
        Placeholder. Replace every TODO-FEE with the actual number before this
        page goes live &mdash; a published fee table is only an advantage if it
        is accurate.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap section">
    <div class="grid grid-2">
      <div>
        <h2 style="margin-top:0">What owners get</h2>
        <ul class="clean">
          <li>Tenant screening covering credit, verified income, rental history, and background</li>
          <li>Marketing across NTREIS and the major syndication sites, with showings handled directly</li>
          <li>Rent collection and a monthly owner statement you can hand to your accountant</li>
          <li>Maintenance coordination through vendors I have used before and will use again</li>
          <li>Texas Property Code compliance on notices, security deposits, and habitability</li>
          <li>Annual rent analysis ahead of renewal, so pricing is a decision rather than a default</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h2 style="margin-top:0">Residential and commercial</h2>
        <p>
          Single-family rentals, small multifamily, and commercial assets are all
          managed in-house. Commercial management is handled by someone who holds
          the TACS designation and reads the lease before enforcing it.
        </p>
        <p><a href="/commercial">Commercial services &rarr;</a></p>

        <h3>Owner portal</h3>
        <p style="margin:0">
          TODO-COPY &mdash; name the management software and link the owner login
          once it is confirmed.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band">
    <div class="wrap section">
      <h2 style="margin-top:0">Common owner questions</h2>
      <h3>Do I have to sign a long contract?</h3>
      <p>TODO-COPY &mdash; state the actual term and cancellation policy.</p>
      <h3>What happens if a tenant stops paying?</h3>
      <p>
        Texas has a defined notice-to-vacate and eviction process with specific
        timelines. I handle the notices, coordinate with counsel where required,
        and keep you informed at each step rather than after the fact.
      </p>
      <h3>Who holds the security deposit?</h3>
      <p>
        Deposits are handled in accordance with Chapter 92 of the Texas Property
        Code, including the accounting and return timelines that apply after a
        tenant moves out.
      </p>
      <h3>Can you manage a property I am not ready to rent yet?</h3>
      <p>TODO-COPY &mdash; answer honestly, including any minimum rent threshold.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band-jade">
    <div class="wrap section">
      <h2 style="margin-top:0">What is my property earning?</h2>
      <p style="max-width:var(--measure)">
        Send me the address and I will tell you what it should rent for today,
        what comparable properties are actually leasing at, and whether managing
        it yourself still makes sense.
      </p>
      <div class="btn-row" style="margin-top:1.75rem">
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/contact">Request a rent analysis</a>
        <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="tel:+19728157644">Call 972-815-7644</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
